    {
      "id": "74daa699-29fd-4124-969b-255f3ffb0ef1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        448,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Lead Data Extraction & Workflow Initialization\n\nThis section initiates the automated email dispatch workflow. It triggers the process based on the configured schedule and fetches lead data from Google Sheets for further processing. The extracted records serve as the input for email validation, verification, delivery handling, and reporting activities in subsequent workflow stages.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b45615df-6960-474f-a826-2dbf93f00ab3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        992,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 672,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Validate and Verify Email Addresses\n\nThis section ensures that only valid email addresses are processed. It first checks for blank email IDs, skips invalid entries, and then verifies the deliverability of the email using an external API (Hunter). Only valid and deliverable emails proceed to the next stage in the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1949df89-8995-4f46-b349-fa3ed33ba3b2",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1712,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 704,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Email Processing & Status Handling\n\nThis section processes the email sending for valid leads. It checks the email’s status (whether it was sent, skipped, or invalid) and updates the Google Sheet accordingly. If the email is valid, it gets sent; otherwise, it is marked as skipped or invalid in the sheet for record-keeping."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b4285390-d1c8-4879-aad3-36402d7a8561",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2464,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 960,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Reporting & Notification\n\nThis section is responsible for consolidating workflow results and generating operational reports. It merges processed data, updates email statuses in the tracking sheet, creates a summarized report of the execution, and sends the final summary notification through Telegram for monitoring and reporting purposes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "71e397da-3434-450d-9e3a-c7a15ad40cac",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -448,
        256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 848,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## How It Works\n\n\"Lead Mail Sending and Report Generation Scheduler\" workflow automates the process of sending emails to leads retrieved from Google Sheets. It checks for blank email IDs, validates email addresses, and verifies their deliverability. Once the emails are verified, it sends emails to valid leads and updates their status in the Google Sheet. After processing, a summary report is generated, counting the total number of sent, skipped, and invalid emails. The summary is then sent via Telegram for quick access.\n\n\n## Setup Steps\n\n1. Prepare Google Sheets\nCreate a Google Sheet with lead data (including emails) to serve as the data source for the workflow.\n\n2. Set Up Email Validation Using Hunter API\nObtain your Hunter API key for email verification to check email validity and deliverability.\n\n3. Connect Accounts in n8n\nAdd credentials for Google Sheets, Hunter, and Telegram to enable data fetching, email verification, and report sending.\n\n4. Add Trigger\nUse the Schedule Trigger node to run the workflow at a set time (e.g., daily) to fetch the latest data from the Google Sheets and begin the email sending process.\n\n5. Fetch Lead Data from Google Sheets\nUse the Google Sheets node to retrieve lead data from the sheet.\n\n6. Validate Email Addresses\nUse the Hunter API node to verify email addresses. Skip invalid or blank emails.\n\n7. Send Emails to Valid Leads\nUse the Gmail/SMTP node to send emails to valid leads, and track their status.\n\n8. Update Email Status in Google Sheets\nUse the Google Sheets node to update the email status for each lead (sent, skipped, invalid).\n\n9. Generate and Merge Email Summary\nUse a Code node to aggregate the results and create a summary.\n\n10. Send Summary Report via Telegram\nSend the summary report with Telegram using the HTTP Request node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
